Reach slicc-kernel's network and file modes from the New Relic CLI on
wasip1.

Reason: wasip1 cannot dial, so every NerdGraph and REST call fails at DNS
(or, with seven's HTTPS_PROXY, at "proxyconnect tcp: dial tcp
127.0.0.1:3128: connect: Connection refused"). internal/slicchost talks to
host/newrelic-host.mjs (newrelic_host probe/call/take) and sets
http.DefaultTransport to it; newrelic-client-go's client (no
HTTPTransport configured) and the CLI's own http.Get calls use that
transport. Requests and response bodies cross as JSON; each body read
yields to other goroutines first. wasip1 mkdir and open pass no mode and
wasip1 chmod does nothing, so ~/.newrelic (0700) and credentials.json
and config.json (0600; credentials.json holds API and license keys) are
set through the host's chmod, the files before anything is written to
them. (newrelic-cli.log is written only by newrelic install, which 0003
refuses.) Upstream asks for 0750 and 0640; on
slicc-kernel the other users of the kernel are not meant to read a user's
keys, so the group bits are dropped too. Without the host module, HTTP
fails with "it needs slicc-kernel with @ai-ecoverse/wasi-newrelic's host
module" and the modes are left alone.

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: wasip1 can dial and set file modes without a host module.

